  {:session/time #time/zdt "2026-10-02T15:30-04:00[America/New_York]",
   :session/image
   "https://cdn.sessionize.com/image/0fc5-400o400o1-XAfqgkLuvXDPWkbzoWron4.png",
   :session/title "The Infrastructure & Growth of Clojars",
   :session/description
   "From this talk, you will learn about Clojars, a critical piece of infrastructure for the Clojure community. You'll learn specifically about:\r\n\r\n- the infrastructure that the Clojars system uses\r\n- the history of Clojars (how did we get here?)\r\n- some statistics about how the Clojars repository has grown over the years (both in usage and deployed libraries)\r\n- recent security improvements to reduce the risk of supply-chain attacks\r\n- some best practices to help defend against potential supply-chain attacks as a library consumer\r\n  \n\n## Toby Crawley\n\nToby is the lead maintainer of Clojars. He has been writing Clojure professionally since 2011, and has maintained Clojars since 2015.",
   :session/external-id "1244725",
   :session/subtitle "Toby Crawley",
   :session/location :location.type/w207abcd,
   :session/type :session.type/session,
   :session/capacity 500,
   :session/duration "PT40M"}
  {:session/time #time/zdt "2026-10-02T16:20-04:00[America/New_York]",
   :session/image
   "https://cdn.sessionize.com/image/e172-400o400o1-YsheEmBHCWiD2n1D9mZ5La.jpg",
   :session/title "How to Make Things, and Why",
   :session/description
   "This is a talk about how to find flow, power, and joy in making software. It is about how to share the love of making with others, and how to nurture and protect communities of makers.\n\n## Stuart Halloway\n\nStuart Halloway is a Distinguished Engineer at Nubank. He is a Clojure committer, and the architect of the Datomic database. Stuart was a founder and President of Cognitect (formerly Relevance).\r\n\r\nStuart has spoken at a variety of industry events, including StrangeLoop, Clojure/conj, EuroClojure, ClojureWest, SpeakerConf, QCon, GOTO, OSCON, RailsConf, RubyConf, JavaOne, and NFJS.\r\n\r\nStuart has written a number of books and technical articles. Of these, he is most proud of Programming Clojure.",
